// Sheet: "persistent control zone moving with the caster" -- explicitly NOT
// a fixed-position zone, unlike every other persistent zone in this batch.
// `StaticAura` (used by cloud_of_daggers/flaming_sphere/web/hunger_of_hadar/
// sleet_storm above) leaves its aura entity BEHIND at the caster's cast-time
// position and does not follow -- the wrong primitive for
// "wheel and flit around the caster". `BasicAura` is the actual match: it
// adds the aura directly onto the CASTER's own entity
// (`AuraChange::Add { entity: data.entity, .. }`, common/src/states/
// basic_aura.rs) rather than spawning a separate positioned entity, so the
// effective zone tracks the caster's position every tick for free -- exactly
// "moves with the caster". Already the precedent for a self-anchored zone in
// this pipeline (transmutation/control_winds_turbulence.ron's own doc
// comment: "BasicAura attaches the aura to the caster's own entity, so the
// zone follows the caster"), just applied here to an enemy-targeted combat
// zone instead of a self-only utility one (see goodberry.ron for this
// batch's own ally-targeted `BasicAura` precedent). Riders: `Slowed`
// ("enemies... are slowed") and `Bleeding` ("take searing harm") both fire
// from the same aura simultaneously, same multi-rider pattern as
// hunger_of_hadar.ron/web.ron. The sheet's necrotic/radiant
// alignment-switchable damage type has no alignment-conditional primitive
// and ships flat as the generic Bleeding drain (same non-elemental-DoT
// choice as cloud_of_daggers.ron/hunger_of_hadar.ron).
BasicAura(
    buildup_duration: 0.6,
    cast_duration: 0.4,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    targets: OutOfGroup,
    auras: [
        (kind: Slowed, strength: 0.5, duration: Some(2), category: Some(Magical)),
        (kind: Bleeding, strength: 5.5, duration: Some(2), category: Some(Magical)),
    ],
    aura_duration: Some(35.0),
    range: 3.0,
    energy_cost: 95.0,
    scales_with_combo: false,
    specifier: None,
    meta: (school: Some(Conjuration), source: Some(Divine)),
)
